Z||000000||ToddAsh||11-05-2000||02:18 PM||||Well I checked everything and all bushings are like new.When I got the car the shocks & struts seemed soft and the back tires were cupped.Swayed bad.Replaced shocks,got alignment,2 new Firestones on rear.Swayed bad.Front tires are original Goodyears with 14,000 miles.I just swapped tires front to rear and the car is perfect. Was the problem the Firestones or the old EAGLES on the front. You guys are great! I'm hooked.I want to sell my '56 Chevy and get a nice GT. Thanks,Todd||||reg||1
Z||000001||Cooter||11-05-2000||03:40 PM||||You actually bought Fierstones? I had a terrible time with Firehawk tires on my full size Cutlass- had a cuss fight with the manager in the showroom full of customers. Even though the front tires were new and the rear tires had less than 20,000 miles on them, they still had a BAD viberation. Bought some cheap wal-mart tires and the problem went away. The Firestone store said the car had at least 2 bent wheels, but they spun true on the balance machine. I hope you have better luck with them than I did.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Oreif||11-05-2000||04:28 PM||||I would have changed all 4 tires. 14 year old tires are most like dry rotted. With daily driving they probably won't last long.||||reg||1
Z||000003||theogre||11-05-2000||04:33 PM||||Have to agree with Oreif. I'd have changed all 4.<P>since you have 2 new ones already I'd get 2 more of the same soon. Those old ones likely have hidden problems developing, especially if they are causing that.||||reg||4
